 :change/help "  sutra change — the path of an ontology change, in four steps\n\n  1 CHANGE\n     change start <title>        Branch AND changeset in one step. The same\n                                 title CONTINUES the open one instead of\n                                 demanding a second branch — one change, one\n                                 branch.\n     …edit your .ent/.enta…\n     change push [-m \"…\"] [--alles] [--trotzdem] [--land]\n                                 THE SAVE. The same checks run LOCALLY FIRST:\n                                 red ⇒ nothing is sent (--trotzdem sends it\n                                 anyway). A bare `git push` asks them too — the\n                                 pre-push hook `start` installs.\n                                 The gates judge BEFORE acceptance:\n                                 red ⇒ nothing moves, with a reason.\n                                 Commits what is STAGED; --alles takes the whole\n                                 tree (a checkout is not always one person's\n                                 work). --land then walks the rest of the ladder\n                                 (ask-review → approve → land) and stops at the\n                                 first refusal.\n     change check [--yes]        Is it usable on the branch? Indexing is compute\n                                 and runs unasked; a build with MODEL CALLS\n                                 shows the price first.\n\n  2 CATCH UP\n     change sync                 Take in the trunk before it catches up with you.\n     change sync --watch [--intervall S]\n                                 Keeps this checkout and the clones below it\n                                 at the instance's state (trunk: fast-forward,\n                                 branch: rebase; a conflict ⇒ nothing moves).\n\n  3 REVIEW\n     change ask-review [--reviewer a,b]\n                                 Preparing → In Review. The push alone asks\n                                 nobody to look.\n     change review [--approve|--reject] [--task T] [--note …]\n                                 Approval falls PER RESOURCE. Without --task the\n                                 verdict counts for all of them.\n\n  4 LAND\n     change land                 The merge IS the save: green checks, every\n                                 resource approved, all or nothing.\n\n  ALWAYS\n     change status [--json]      Where am I, why does it (not) go through, whom\n                                 does it hit, what runs afterwards. Writes\n                                 nothing.\n     change explain check <rule>   What a rule means, in plain words.\n\n  Everywhere: --dir PATH (another clone) · --offline (never the network) · --lang de|en.\n  Exit 0 = nothing blocks · 1 = an error · 2 = state unknown.\n  Everything operational — manual builds, retention, access — is `sutra`."
