 :change/rule-aktion-function-rule-bedingung "The action's FUNCTION RULE does not conform: it names no function or an unknown one, it stands beside other rules, or the action declares no `:edits`."
 :change/rule-aktion-function-rule-hinweis "the function's code performs every change itself. And because its edits only come into being at runtime, NOTHING can be derived from the rule: `:edits` is the only statement about what the action may touch, is therefore mandatory, and the run is measured against it (an edit outside it aborts the action)."
 :change/rule-aktion-phantom-edit-bedingung
   "The action declares something in `:edits` that none of its rules carries out."
 :change/rule-aktion-phantom-edit-hinweis "`:edits` is provenance, not a declaration of intent: it has to be a subset of what the rules mutate. The platform has always enforced that on install — but until now without saying WHICH action was meant."
 :change/rule-aktion-unbekannter-parametertyp-bedingung "An action parameter has a `:type` that is neither a storable value type nor a declared object/link type."
 :change/rule-aktion-unbekannter-parametertyp-hinweis "Parametric types (`[:decimal p s]`) pass — the grammar checks their shape. Only the case where a simple name points at nothing is checked. Together with its three siblings this covers `actions-valid?` completely: the same conditions, but with a subject."
 :change/rule-aktion-unbekannter-typ-bedingung "An action rule (`:create`/`:update`/`:delete-object`, `:create-link`/`:delete-link`) names an object or link type that does not exist."
 :change/rule-aktion-unbekannter-typ-hinweis "Only LITERAL type names are checked — where a parameter stands (`[:get :arg0 …]`), the type is known only at runtime and the rule is skipped. Without this check the typo installs green and only shows up for the first user who submits the action."
 :change/rule-aktion-unbekanntes-ziel-bedingung "The action's `:target` names neither a declared object nor a link type — or does not have the shape of a target at all."
 :change/rule-aktion-unbekanntes-ziel-hinweis "Three spellings are admissible: a bare name, `{:target-object-type …}` and `{:target-link-type …}`. The installation reads anything else as “no target” and creates an action that points at nothing."
 :change/rule-datei-unlesbar-bedingung
   "The `.ent` file is not readable EDN — usually an unbalanced paren."
 :change/rule-datei-unlesbar-hinweis "Until it reads, NOTHING can be said about its content: the resources in it are missing from every other section of this screen."
 :change/rule-einreichung-check-bedingung
   "A server-side check of the pushed commit stands at `failed`."
 :change/rule-formular-handgebaut-bedingung "An app builds an Action's input fields itself instead of letting the form be generated from the Action definition."
 :change/rule-formular-handgebaut-hinweis "`:action-form` does the same. It does not block — but the fields drift from the Action the moment either side changes."
 :change/soll-form-from-action "the form comes from the Action definition"
 :change/fix-use-action-form "`{:widget :action-form :action <name>}` instead of input widgets plus `:action-button` — type, label, requiredness and constraints already live on the Action."
 :change/rule-einreichung-check-hinweis "The commit IS in git and did NOT take effect. Fix it and push again — a second push of the same state does not run through the gates ('Everything up-to-date')."
 :change/rule-geltung-fremde-sektion-bedingung "The file declares a section this repository does not carry: types belong to the ontology, code to the code repository."
 :change/rule-geltung-fremde-sektion-hinweis "The `scope` check refuses the push instead of silently discarding the foreign section — a push that half takes effect would be the worst outcome."
 :change/rule-grammatik-verletzt-bedingung "The entry does not fit the `.ent` grammar (sutra.parser.ent/EntFile) — unknown key, missing required key or wrong type."
 :change/rule-grammatik-verletzt-hinweis "The same closed grammar `ci/sutra-publish` checks the push against. What is red here is red there."
 :change/rule-neubau-logik-ohne-version-bedingung "The computing part of an incremental transform (`:code`/`:query`/`:code-file`) changed, `:semantic-version` did not."
 :change/rule-neubau-logik-ohne-version-hinweis "An incremental run sees only new rows; the old ones keep yesterday's answer. Only a `:semantic-version` bump forces the full run that applies the changed logic to the existing rows."
 :change/rule-neubau-schlüssel-migration-bedingung
   "An object type's `:match-keys` have changed — the DECLARATION of identity."
 :change/rule-neubau-schlüssel-migration-hinweis "On an ordinary type `:match-keys` is not the key: ids are minted from the primary producer's `:primary-key` (`:match-keys` only takes effect with `:resolve-entity true`). Where the two disagree, the install refuses the push (`identity-inert`) — a composite grain has to arrive as a COMPUTED column in the shaping transform. And if the minting really moves: send it as a pair, bump `:semantic-version` (forces one full run) AND `:write-mode :replace` (makes the run authoritative, so the reconcile phase retires what it omits)."
 :change/rule-quelle-klartext-geheimnis-bedingung
   "A `:sources` entry carries `:secrets` or `:secret-cipher` in the tree."
 :change/rule-quelle-klartext-geheimnis-hinweis "A push carrying credentials is refused. The connector belongs in the tree, the secret exactly once in the platform: `source secret <name>`."
 :change/rule-referenz-ungelöst-bedingung "A name points at nothing: a rollup `:over`, an `:implements`, a `:satisfies`, an action parameter or an agent reference without a target."
 :change/rule-referenz-ungelöst-hinweis "Locally this resolves against the file (closed world, as far as the section is declared). A reference to something that exists ONLY on prod counts as open here — the push resolves against live ∪ desired."
 :change/rule-referenz-verdächtig-bedingung
   "Heuristic: an SQL column does not resolve against the inputs, or a link has no producer."
 :change/rule-referenz-verdächtig-hinweis
   "Never blocks — a link filled by an action is legal, and the SQL scan is deliberately coarse."
