 :change/fix-stale-base "`sutra change start \"<title>\"` branches fresh off origin/main and carries these edits over; on a branch with an open changeset `sutra change sync` does the same."
 :change/rule-veralteter-zweig-bedingung
   "The tree carries uncommitted edits, and the branch they were made on sits behind the trunk."
 :change/rule-veralteter-zweig-hinweis "A `git pull --ff-only` reports 'Fast-forward' and thereby proves NOTHING about the distance to main — it advances the branch you are standing on. Editing on a leftover branch declares every resource the trunk has gained since to be deleted: one carrying user edits is refused by the gate; one without vanishes silently."
 :change/ist-ent-in-git "{n} `.ent` text(s) changed: {pfade}"
 :change/soll-ent-ueber-cli "changed through `sutra projection pull/push` — git carries Python"
 :change/fix-ent-ueber-cli "`sutra --branch <branch> projection pull <projection> <text> --to /abs/path`, edit, `projection push /abs/path/<text> --preview`, then without `--preview`. `git stash` keeps this working copy until you no longer need it."
 :change/rule-ebene-ent-nicht-in-git-bedingung
   "The change touches a `.ent` text — the plane the instance holds, not git's."
 :change/rule-ebene-ent-nicht-in-git-hinweis "git carries Python; every `.ent` text is a projection of the ontology. A git push installs the WHOLE tree and thereby declares deleted every resource the trunk has gained since — which is why the server refuses it, and why this gate no longer judges the texts' content. `projection push` merges per element over the base of your `pull` and touches only what the projection showed. Committed this is an error; in the working tree alone it is a warning, because a push sends commits."
 :change/rule-sql-char-bedingung
   "A SQL transform casts to CHAR without a length (`CAST(x AS CHAR)`, `x::char`)."
 :change/rule-sql-char-hinweis "In Postgres a bare CHAR is char(1): every value is silently cut to its first character — no error, just wrong keys."
 :change/rule-sql-abgelehnt-bedingung "Postgres, the store the transform runs on, does not compile the SQL (EXPLAIN against the LIVE inputs)."
 :change/rule-sql-abgelehnt-hinweis
   "The build would die on exactly this message. DuckDB/MySQL spellings are not Postgres."
 :change/rule-sql-ungeprueft-bedingung "The SQL could not be compiled against Postgres — an input does not exist yet, or the instance did not answer."
